<subpara id="RM0000005GN00VX_z0" proc-id="RM0550J___0000A1200000">
<content5 releasenbr="1">
<step1>
<ptxt>ECU Data Monitor</ptxt>
<step2>
<ptxt>Using SST (TaSCAN), the input, communication and operating status of the steering lock ECU can be read.</ptxt>
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09991-70200</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<step3>
<ptxt>Connect SST (TaSCAN) to DLC3 and turn the IG ON.</ptxt>
</step3>
<step3>
<ptxt>On the SST (TaSCAN) screen, select [Diagnosis] → [System Diagnosis/Body] → [System Name/Certification ECU (Steering Lock)] → [ECU Data], and select the item to be checked.</ptxt>
<atten3>
<list1 type="unordered">
<item>
<ptxt>Since the steering lock ECU responds to SST (TaSCAN) via the CAN communication function of the certification ECU, monitoring may not be performed normally if there is a malfunction in CAN communication or the certification ECU.</ptxt>
</item>
<item>
<ptxt>When checking diagnostic trouble codes or data monitor related to the smart entry &amp; start system from the IG OFF state, the main body may not respond unless any door is opened to cancel its sleep state.</ptxt>
</item>
</list1>
</atten3>
</step3>
</step2>
<step2>
<ptxt>ECU Data Monitor</ptxt>
<step3>
<ptxt>Using TaSCAN, perform the ECU Data Monitor to determine whether the system is OK or NG and narrow down the malfunctioning area.</ptxt>
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09991-70200</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
